      "side": 1,
      "message": "Naming quibbles (and this is all in nit territory):\n\"connect preconnected\" just sounds weird. We don\u0027t really pre-connect; we generate the socket connections on demand. It\u0027s only from the point of view of the code inside binder that the sockets are connected by us not it.\nrequest_fd should probably be called fd_factory, socket_factory, connection_factory?\nAnd maybe the function should be connect_rpc_binder_with_factory, or something?\n\n(Obviously that implies RpcPreconnectedClient is also a bad name, but meh.)",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 42,
        "startChar": 0,
        "endLine": 44,
        "endChar": 39
